From f6328c2e634cdfd881688d993650e32bdebd3654 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vladimir Skvortsov <vskvortsov@emcraft.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 12:54:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: imx6sx: take the FEC1 reference clock from the pad

imx6sx_enet_clk_sel() clears both the FEC clock mux select and the pad
direction unconditionally at machine init. That is right for the RGMII
reference designs, where the PHY has its own crystal, and wrong for an RMII
board where the PHY supplies the 50 MHz reference back to the SoC -- GPR1[13]
has to select the external clock.

Nothing needs to set IMX6SX_CLK_ENET_REF: with bit 13 set the reference
arrives on the pad, so the SoC's internal ENET_REF is not the source and its
rate does not matter. The link comes up at 100/full with no rate assignment
in the device tree.

Because it runs at machine init it also overwrites whatever the bootloader
configured, so it cannot be worked around from the device tree or from
U-Boot. The in-tree i.MX6SX RMII boards, udoo-neo and softing-vining-2000,
carry no clock configuration for it either.

Without it the PHY never answers MDIO, and the FEC's phy-connect error path
then corrupts the slab: the kernel oopses in kmem_cache_alloc about five
seconds later, in whatever allocates next.

The patch is applied only to this machine's kernel, so it sets the bit
unconditionally; a change for the kernel itself would key it on the FEC's
phy-mode.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Vladimir Skvortsov <vskvortsov@emcraft.com>
---
 arch/arm/mach-imx/mach-imx6sx.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-imx/mach-imx6sx.c b/arch/arm/mach-imx/mach-imx6sx.c
index b57d54a..35f16e2 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-imx/mach-imx6sx.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-imx/mach-imx6sx.c
@@ -20,8 +20,15 @@ static void __init imx6sx_enet_clk_sel(void)
 
 	gpr = syscon_regmap_lookup_by_compatible("fsl,imx6sx-iomuxc-gpr");
 	if (!IS_ERR(gpr)) {
+		/*
+		 * FEC1 is RMII with the PHY driving the 50 MHz reference back
+		 * into the SoC, so GPR1[13] selects the external clock. This
+		 * runs at machine init, after the bootloader, so it has the
+		 * final say.
+		 */
 		regmap_update_bits(gpr, IOMUXC_GPR1,
-				   IMX6SX_GPR1_FEC_CLOCK_MUX_SEL_MASK, 0);
+				   IMX6SX_GPR1_FEC_CLOCK_MUX_SEL_MASK,
+				   0x1 << 13);
 		regmap_update_bits(gpr, IOMUXC_GPR1,
 				   IMX6SX_GPR1_FEC_CLOCK_PAD_DIR_MASK, 0);
 	} else {
-- 
